Although the `_set_read_only()` method being empty is rather meh. We could bind a virtual method  (with `BIND_VMETHOD`) and call it:
```C++
void EditorProperty::_set_read_only(bool p_read_only) {
	if (get_script_instance() && get_script_instance()->has_method("_set_read_only")) {
		get_script_instance()->call("_set_read_only", p_type);
	}
}
```
This way the behavior could be customized from plugins. (and it also means that you'd need to restore the base method calls...)

